From e2f7ce884de12748b5fc02edf6f9f4fc4e8ebe00 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DoubleGate <parobek@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 04:06:04 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] [UPSTREAM] analysis: plumb ML1 measurements to analyzers
 (T-OR-058)

Physical-layer ML1 serving/neighbor cell measurements (PCI, EARFCN, RSRP)
are decoded by the diag layer but never reached analyzers: they are not
GSMTAP-convertible, so analyze_qmdl_message reported them as skipped packets.

Add an analyzer-facing `Ml1Measurement` (serving cell / neighbor cells,
decoupled from the on-wire deku structs, carrying no subscriber identity) with
`from_log_body`, a new default-no-op `Analyzer::report_measurement` trait
method (mirroring report_skipped_packet, so existing analyzers are unaffected),
a Harness fan-out, and an analyze_qmdl_message dispatch that surfaces the two
ML1 log bodies (0xb17f serving, 0xb180 neighbor) before the GSMTAP path.

The ML1 branch also calls report_skipped_packet so time-based analyzers keep
advancing their clock on these packets as they did before the branch existed
(the measurement event takes each analyzer's slot, falling back to the time
tick) -- otherwise a time-based detector would silently stop seeing ML1 packets.

This is additive and backward-compatible -- no public enum changes -- and is
the measurement input a cell-identity-consistency analyzer (T-OR-059) consumes.
Tests: from_log_body matches the diag ml1 vectors (pci/earfcn/rsrp), a
serving-cell log reaches report_measurement while a non-ML1 log does not, and
ML1-only packets still make a time-based analyzer fire at its threshold.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
